@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 0. Register the user used by the requests below (run once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.smith@example.com",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

### 1. Log in and capture the JWT token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.smith@example.com",
  "password": "super-secret-1"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 2. Create a meeting and capture its id
# @name createMeeting
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Sprint planning",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-10-01T10:00:00.000Z"
}

###
@meetingId = {{createMeeting.response.body.id}}

### 3. Upload a recording (-> 201 Created, status "processing")
# Put a real mp3 / wav / m4a / mp4 / webm next to this file and adjust the path below.
# Allowed: mp3, wav, m4a, mp4, webm; max 100 MiB (UPLOAD_MAX_RECORDING_SIZE).
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingId}}/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----RecordingBoundary

------RecordingBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="meeting.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< ./meeting.mp3
------RecordingBoundary--

### 4. Read the recording metadata and status (-> 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingId}}/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Upload a second recording to the same meeting (-> 409 Conflict until replacement is implemented)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingId}}/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----RecordingBoundary

------RecordingBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="meeting.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< ./meeting.mp3
------RecordingBoundary--

### 6. Upload an unsupported format (-> 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingId}}/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----RecordingBoundary

------RecordingBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="document.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.4 not a recording
------RecordingBoundary--

### 7. Upload without a token (-> 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingId}}/recording
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----RecordingBoundary

------RecordingBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="meeting.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< ./meeting.mp3
------RecordingBoundary--

### 8. Read the recording of a non-existent meeting (-> 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meetings/000000000000000000000000/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Read the recording with an invalid meeting id (-> 400 Bad Request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meetings/not-a-valid-id/recording
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
